Sval: ContentSearch answers only pages still there

A page's `GetEngine` waits on the search service before it reads the
actor's browsing context, and a page closed in that time has a destroyed
actor, whose `browsingContext` throws InvalidStateError. Sval closes the
startup tab's home page as soon as a restored workspace has tabs of its
own, so this would happen on most launches. The reply checks the actor is
still registered (`didDestroy` removes it), in `_reply` for every message.

A page navigated to another process keeps its child actor until its old
process tears the page down, so a reply the parent sent before the page left
can arrive when `contentWindow` is null, and `Cu.cloneInto` throws on it.
The child drops a message that finds no window.

